From 6e3c39d610c9537a6e03726ec1dd58029b1e3313 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rongkunxue <rongkunxue@outlook.com>
Date: Wed, 15 Jul 2026 20:32:24 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] [fsdp] fix: sync merged LoRA weights before context exit
 (#7014)

This PR fixes a stale-weight bug in the FSDP LoRA rollout weight sync
path when `actor_rollout_ref.model.lora.merge=True`.

Before this change, `FSDPEngine.get_per_tensor_param()` built a
`state_dict()` inside `merged_lora_context()`, but returned a lazy
iterator that was consumed only after the context had already exited.
Since `state_dict()` tensors alias the live module parameter storage,
and `merged_lora_context()` restores the un-merged base weights on exit,
the rollout engine could silently receive base weights without the LoRA
delta.

As a result, vLLM rollout weights stopped tracking the latest actor LoRA
updates after the first step. In affected runs,
`training/rollout_probs_diff_mean` kept increasing step by step, while
`rollout_actor_probs_pearson_corr` gradually dropped and rewards did not
improve.

This PR keeps the merged LoRA context alive until every tensor is
materialized and yielded to the rollout weight sync consumer.

Relevant issue: https://github.com/verl-project/verl/issues/6782

This does not duplicate an existing PR because issue #6782 currently has
no linked PR on GitHub, and the following duplicate-work searches did
not show an existing open PR for the same fix:

- https://github.com/verl-project/verl/pulls?q=is%3Apr+is%3Aopen+6782
-
https://github.com/verl-project/verl/pulls?q=is%3Apr+is%3Aopen+merged_lora_context
-
https://github.com/verl-project/verl/pulls?q=is%3Apr+is%3Aopen+lora+merge+rollout+weight+sync

### Test

This change has been tested and verified to resolve
[#6782](https://github.com/verl-project/verl/issues/6782).

- `PATH="$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH" .venv/bin/pre-commit run --all-files
--show-diff-on-failure --color=never`
- `pytest -q tests/workers/test_engine_workers_lora_sync.py` (16 passed)

Full reproduction logs, validation results, and training behavior will
be synchronized to the corresponding issue.

### API and Usage Example

No API or config changes.

The existing `actor_rollout_ref.model.lora.merge=True` path now sends
the merged base + LoRA weights correctly during rollout weight sync.

### Design & Code Changes

The root cause is that the previous merge path created a `state_dict()`
inside `merged_lora_context()`, but materialized the tensors only after
leaving the context. Since the context restores the original base
weights on exit, the lazy consumer could receive restored base weights
instead of merged LoRA weights.

This PR changes the merged LoRA path to stream weights through a
dedicated generator:

- Keep `merged_lora_context(self.module, backup_adapters=True)` open
inside the generator.
- Normalize and convert weight keys while the merged weights are active.
- Materialize `DTensor` values with `full_tensor()` before yielding
them.
- Clone plain tensors before yielding to avoid aliasing with restored
module storage.
- Move FSDP parameter offload into a `finally` block so offload happens
after the generator is fully consumed.

The unmerged LoRA path (`merge=False`) and non-LoRA path are unchanged.

AI assistance was used to help draft this PR description. The human
submitter reviewed every changed line, validated the behavior, and is
responsible for the final PR.

